        <zone h='31222' id='9' name='Japan Purchase Rate by AGE_SEG' w='45300' x='1300' y='22222'>
          <layout-cache minheight='183' type-h='scalable' type-w='cell' />
        </zone>
        <zone h='30667' id='15' name='Japan Customers by AGE_SEG' w='45800' x='1700' y='53667' />
        <zone h='29778' id='16' name='Japan Purchase Rate by Gender' w='47300' x='52600' y='54889' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='13444' id='17' type-v2='text' w='89900' x='2000' y='85778'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>INSIGHT</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Japan purchase rate is 57.6% (23,031 of 40,000).</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Purchase rises sharply with car age: 36.4% in AGE_SEG 1 vs 84.0% in AGE_SEG 4.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>That is the pattern transferred to India: prioritize AGE_SEG 3 and 4 in CRM.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Japan has a purchase label. India has model scores only.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Calibri' fontsize='11'>Do not treat raw India income as the same unit as Japan income.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='30111' id='38' name='Buyers vs Non-Buyers' w='43600' x='53300' y='21444' />
        <zone h='10889' id='39' name='KPIs-4' show-title='false' w='92500' x='5600' y='7444' />
